From bf315fdfc1786954469dd65cf7d6b27feed0c53b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:59:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0196: the stock codec clocks and RX macro table
 (topaz), beeps over ssh

0195 on the phone: L14 on, everything powered, nothing heard, not even
from the headphones. ios-topaz / topaz-woa (same SoC, same WCD937x AUX
path) only heard sound once they did as stock Android does: ask the DSP
for the TX core/NPL clocks only and leave the RX MCLK mux at 0 (RX and VA
run on the TX MCLK), start the TX macro's clocks, pulse the SoundWire
CGCRs, and write the 119 RX macro registers of a stock dump taken while
playing. All that here, with the stock WCD937x values; the headphones
only on request.

kern.sweet_audio (bsd/dev/sweet_audio_ctl.c) hands requests to the ADSP
thread: beeps on the graph the 45 s test leaves open, register reads and
writes (WCD937x, RX/VA macros, SoundWire masters and slave, FS1815), the
whole test again, and flags that bring back the 0195 ways one by one.
